{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q76428523","formula":"C₁₉H₂₇N₃O","hill":"C19H27N3O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":19.0,"H":27.0,"N":3.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"NDTDI"},"descriptions":{"en":"NDTDI, also known as 9-desmethine-LSD, 9-nor-LSD, or 8,10-seco-LSD, is a psychedelic drug related to lysergic acid diethylamide (LSD). It is a tricyclic cyclized tryptamine and partial lysergamide and is a structurally simplified analogue of LSD. The drug is specifically the analogue of LSD in which the carbon atom at position 9 of the ergoline ring system has been removed. It has been reported to produce psychedelic effects similarly to LSD, but with much lower potency."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":163192742,"mass":313.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCN(CC)C(=O)CCN(C)C1CC2=C3C(=CNC3=CC=C2)C1","inchikey":"JECGWOMOCPQHDH-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"N,N-diethyl-3-[methyl(1,3,4,5-tetrahydrobenzo[cd]indol-4-yl)amino]propanamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"163192742","atoms":50,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-5.639,"y":-0.899,"z":0.671,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.773,"y":-0.822,"z":-0.575,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.793,"y":0.268,"z":-0.528,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.238,"y":1.599,"z":-0.948,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.664,"y":2.487,"z":0.212,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.502,"y":0.154,"z":-0.003,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.769,"y":1.138,"z":0.109,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.059,"y":-1.232,"z":0.448,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.613,"y":-1.276,"z":0.966,"el":"C"},{"x":0.359,"y":-1.565,"z":-0.117,"el":"N"},{"x":0.443,"y":-3.015,"z":-0.33,"el":"C"},{"x":1.691,"y":-0.936,"z":0.154,"el":"C"},{"x":1.6,"y":0.639,"z":-0.029,"el":"C"},{"x":2.934,"y":1.319,"z":0.151,"el":"C"},{"x":4.078,"y":0.566,"z":-0.114,"el":"C"},{"x":4.145,"y":-0.78,"z":-0.512,"el":"C"},{"x":5.479,"y":-1.087,"z":-0.648,"el":"C"},{"x":6.202,"y":0.05,"z":-0.337,"